-- title:
--   Constant reduction of a constant-field extension of function fields
-- statement:
--   Let $K$, $F$, $K'$, $F'$ be fields with $F$ a $K$-algebra, $F'$ a $K'$-algebra, $K'$ a $K$-algebra, $F'$ an $F$-algebra and an $K$-algebra, the two towers $K \subseteq K' \subseteq F'$ and $K \subseteq F \subseteq F'$ being compatible (`IsScalarTower`), and let $K$ be algebraically closed. Assume: (`hfg`) there is $x \in F$ transcendental over $K$ such that $F$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $K(x)$; (`hfg'`) there is $x \in F'$ transcendental over $K'$ such that $F'$ is finite-dimensional over $K'(x)$; and (`hgen`) the intermediate field of $F'/K'$ generated by $K'$ together with the image of $F$ in $F'$ is all of $F'$. Then there exist a valuation subring $\mathcal O$ of $F'$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho \colon \mathcal O \to F$ such that: every $f \in F$ has its image in $F'$ lying in $\mathcal O$, with $\rho$ of that element equal to $f$; the kernel of $\rho$ is the maximal ideal of the local ring $\mathcal O$; for every $f' \in F'$ with $f' \neq 0$ there is a scalar $c \in K'$ with $c \cdot f' \in \mathcal O$ and $\rho(c \cdot f') \neq 0$; and for every $c \in K'$ whose image in $F'$ lies in $\mathcal O$, the value $\rho(c)$ lies in the image of $K$ in $F$.
--
--   This is the existence of a regular constant reduction, in the sense of Deuring and Roquette, of the constant-field extension $F' = K'\!\cdot\!F$ of an algebraic function field $F$ of one variable over an algebraically closed constant field $K$: the reduction has residue field exactly $F$, is unramified with respect to the constants (third clause), and carries constants to constants (fourth clause). It is used in the comparison of divisor orders under constant-field extension, via [`AlgebraicCurve.Divisor.exists_natCast_dvd_ord_sub_of_constantFieldExtension`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.Divisor.exists_natCast_dvd_ord_sub_of_constantFieldExtension).
